# Copy to ~/.config/comfy-i2v-env/private-strings and fill in.
# NEVER commit the filled-in file: it is a list of exactly the strings that must
# not become public, so committing it would be the leak it prevents.
#
# One string per line. Matching is case-insensitive and substring-based.
# Good candidates:
#
#   - the build machine's login name (leaks through /home paths and caches)
#   - the machine's hostname
#   - any real name
#   - any personal email address
#   - private repository or project names that should not be linked to this one
#   - internal hostnames or LAN addresses
